1. What Is ST-T1024?
ST-T1024 is an open, Apache-2.0 standard for deterministic AI inference on embedded and
edge hardware. It replaces stochastic transformer inference with a fully deterministic,
FSM-orchestrated, ternary-quantized pipeline.
The Standard specifies:
· A 6-step deterministic inference pipeline
· Ternary logic ({-1, 0, +1}) with XNOR + popcount arithmetic
· Hardware-enforced Assured Execution Time (AET) ≤ 800 ns
· 75% immutable ROM / 25% sovereign-updatable SRAM
· Air-gapped execution (no cloud dependency)
· SK-1024 sovereign update protocol (National Authority control)
