3. Certification Readiness
ST-T1024's architecture was designed to satisfy the technical requirements shared across
the four foundational safety and security norms.
Standard Domain. Key Requirement. ST-T1024 Status
ISO 26262 Automotive Determinism, Freedom from Interference, Traceability ✅
Architecturally aligned; ASIL-D path
IEC 61508 Industrial Systematic Capability, Fail-Safe Operation ✅ Credible path to SIL 3
DO-178C Aerospace Determinism, No External Dependencies ✅ Fits standard "as written";
DAL B path
IEC 62443 Cybersecurity Isolation, Tamper Resistance, Restricted Data Flow ✅
Hardware-enforced; SL 3 ready
IEC 62304 Medical Software Safety Class, Risk Control ✅ Determinism supports safety
classification
The Unifying Insight: All four standards demand the same architectural properties:
determinism, traceability, isolation, immutability, and fail-safety.
ST-T1024 was built to embody these properties from the start. Certification in one domain
accelerates certification in others.
