4. Silicon Implementation Path
ST-T1024 has been validated in emulation. The path to physical silicon is documented and
cost-estimated:
Phase Platform Goal Estimated Cost Phase 1 FPGA (Sapphire TJ375, Xilinx ML605) Validate architecture in hardware
$5,000–$50,000
Phase 2 Hybrid (T1024 + FPGA co-processor) Real-world embedded validation
$5,000–$20,000
Phase 3 65nm ASIC Production silicon $220,000–$500,000
Total Program Cost: ~$250,000–$600,000 for a complete silicon proof-of-concept.
Sovereignty: Designed for RISC-V—open, royalty-free, any nation can implement without
dependency on foreign IP.
